Ollama is a CLI (command line interface) tool that makes it easy to run open source llms, its like docker for llm, supports model like Msitral ,LLAMA 3, Gemma, code llama etc. 

>>Install:-
1)install WSL(window subsytem for linux,its feature of wndows that allows users to run a linux environment directly on Windows wohtout need for visual machien or dual booting) - https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/window/wsl/install
2) OR winget install --id Ollama.Ollama      write in terminal for windows 
curl -fsSL https:ollama.com/install.sh | sh  write in terminal for mac/linux

>>Use , in terminal:-
-ollama
-ollama run tinyllama - (to run small model called tinyllama, it is only of 686MB)
-ask question   - What is artificial intelligence?
-/bye 

>>use ollama via api (our Python code, Node.js program, or another application sends a request to the model and receives its response.)Suppose you're building your ESP32 voice assistant.With direct chat, you type a question manually.With the API, your Python program can send the transcribed speech to Ollama and receive the AI's answer automatically.
- by default , it runs on http://localhost:11434/api/generate

Paste in temrinal to test :curl.exe -X POST "http://localhost:11434/api/generate" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"model\":\"tinyllama\",\"prompt\":\"What is the capital of India?\",\"stream\":false}"

In python :-
1)First install the required library in CMD: py -m pip install requests
2)Usually, Ollama starts automatically in the background when you install and launch it on Windows.
3)Then run your Python file: py ask_ai.py
4)Python code:-
  
import requests

response = requests.post(
    "http://localhost:11434/api/generate",
    json={
        "model": "tinyllama",
        "prompt": "What is the capital of India?",
        "stream": False
    }
)

answer = response.json()["response"]
print(answer)

>Example :
1)You speak
2)ESP32 sends audio to laptop
3)Python converts speech into text
4)Using speech recognition, such as Whisper
5)Python calls the Ollama API
6)Sends the question to TinyLlama
7)Python receives the AI answer
8)Text-to-speech reads the answer aloud

>>Modelfile:- in Ollama is like a set of instructions for creating your own customized model from an existing model.
1. Create a Modelfile on Windows :Open Notepad and write:  (File name: Modelfile , Save as type: All Files  ,Choose a folder, such as C:\OllamaTest  )
  FROM tinyllama
  SYSTEM "You are a friendly AI assistant. Explain computer science concepts in simple English and use short examples."
  PARAMETER temperature 0.7
2. Use your Modelfile
  Open CMD:
  cd C:\OllamaTest
  ollama create myassistant -f Modelfile       //This creates a customized Ollama model named myassistant.
  ollama run myassistant                        //this run the modelfile
  Explain Python loops to me.                   //Ask a question, Your model will follow the system instructions you added, as far as its capabilities allow.
3.You can use your custom model through the same API as before. Just change the model name in your Python code, 
     "model": "myassistant",

